    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI'm trying to integrate a french grammar linter (grammalecte) into a plugin (nvim-lint).\n\nWhen `vim.diagnostic` display the error position, if there is a accentuated character, the issue is displayed one character early (and so on for any other accentuated character).\n\nthe warning obtained through `vim.diagnostic.get`\n```\n_extmark_id = 5,\nbufnr = 1,\ncol = 53,\nend_col = 55,\nend_lnum = 6,\nlnum = 6,\nmessage = \"Apostrophe typographique.\",\nnamespace = 44,\nseverity = 2,\nsource = \"grammalecte\"\n```\n\nthe warning position\n<img width=\"547\" height=\"31\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98a0a732-6cb2-44b4-ada2-8122ed8ad1a7\" />\n\nHow it is marked (should be on the `l'`)\n<img width=\"682\" height=\"35\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1ce8c1e-58a1-4ff3-af14-e34430286caa\" />\n\nWhen I remove all accentuated characters before the error\n<img width=\"669\" height=\"38\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f071944-6aa6-4599-9923-4a77f64fe14d\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nadd an error through vim.diagnostic on any element of the line after accentuated character.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nHave the error marked where it is.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-3938+g9ff302d0ca\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nI don't know\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot 1.27.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nfoot\n\n### Installation\n\nfrom git repository",
